<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-field-index-base="/field-index/"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><meta name="color-scheme" content="light" /><meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f0e7" /><meta name="description" content="Coreweaver Field Index methodology for source-led agentic AI infrastructure records." /><link rel="canonical" href={canonical} /><link rel="icon" href="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin /><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,500;6..72,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" /><link rel="stylesheet" href="/field-index/assets/field-index.css" /><title>Methodology — Coreweaver Field Index</title></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#methodology">Skip to methodology</a><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/field-index" aria-label="Coreweaver Field Index home"><img src="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" /><span><strong>COREWEAVER</strong><small>FIELD INDEX / 001</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Field Index navigation"><a href="/field-index">Index</a><a href="/field-index/editorial-policy">Editorial policy</a><a href="/">Coreweaver Labs ↗</a></nav></header><main class="content-main" id="methodology"><div class="section-kicker"><span>02</span> Methodology</div><h1>Evidence held <em>open to inspection.</em></h1><p class="content-lede">The Field Index is a hand-curated public reference. Its purpose is to name what a source supports, show how it was interpreted, and leave space for a correction when the evidence changes.</p><section class="content-block"><h2>What inclusion means</h2><p>Inclusion means an editor reviewed a named public source and wrote a constrained description of its relevance to agentic AI infrastructure. It does not imply that a record is important, safe, compatible, compliant, funded, independent, endorsed, affiliated with Coreweaver Labs, or better than a record that is not listed.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>Record requirements</h2><div class="content-table-wrap"><table class="content-table"><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Why it is visible</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Primary source</td><td>Lets a reader examine the evidence directly rather than relying solely on a summary.</td></tr><tr><td>Last verified</td><td>Signals when the editor last checked the source and supports future re-review.</td></tr><tr><td>Scope note</td><td>Explains the narrow reason the record belongs in this field reference.</td></tr><tr><td>Relationship label</td><td>Distinguishes public ecosystem links from affiliation, implementation, or endorsement.</td></tr><tr><td>Caveat</td><td>States what the cited material does not establish.</td></tr><tr><td>Change log</td><td>Creates a visible record of material updates or corrections.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="content-block"><h2>Review sequence</h2><p>An editor first identifies a primary public source, then writes only the claim the source supports. The record is checked for claim drift, relation labels, current verification date, and a plain-language caveat. If a source is unavailable, changes materially, or does not support the summary, the entry should be narrowed, annotated, or removed rather than padded with inference.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>Limits of the Index</h2><p>The Index is not an audit, security test, certification, benchmark, market map, directory, or legal assessment. It will contain omissions and may not reflect every meaningful workstream. Readers should open original sources and make their own context-sensitive assessment before relying on a record.</p><a class="text-link" href="/field-index/editorial-policy">Read editorial policy <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section></main><footer><div class="footer__brand"><img src="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" alt="" width="36" height="36" /><span>COREWEAVER FIELD INDEX / 001</span></div><p>Source-led infrastructure records for an accountable agentic AI field.</p><a href="/field-index">Return to Index ↗</a></footer></body></html>
